      "math_academy_id": "q-117143",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191213/assets/6239a47a2bd88b631f9058c7afe3b59c10b8e71fb8957fe7a354cc7e72daf69d.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠BOC={72}^{∘}$ and $m∠AOC=7x+{9}^{∘}.$ If $\\overset{\\to }{OC}$ is the bisector of $∠AOB,$ find the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191213/assets/6a49c1d69a34d0159cd24869b51cb7a517021a147e0e831b969c1135f6b533fc.png)\n\nThe bisector of an angle divides the angle into two congruent angles. Thus, $∠AOC≅∠BOC.$ Therefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOC & =m∠BOC \\\\ 7x+{9}^{∘} & ={72}^{∘} \\\\ 7x & ={63}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={9}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
